hexa -- hexagonal Sokoban=========================    hexa [level]Push every moneybag ($) onto a safe square (.) on a six-sided grid, bywalking into it -- you can only push a bag, never pull it, and only oneat a time, so a bag shoved into a corner is stuck.  Walls (#) block you.Solve it in as few moves as you can.Because the grid is hexagonal each cell has six neighbours, so there aresix move keys:        k  up    u  \  /  i           upleft / upright        \/        /\    n  /  \  m           downleft / downright        j  down`q' quits.  `hexa <level>' opens the built-in level editor for thatscreen: place walls, bags, safes and your start with the same keys, then`q' saves it.  Five screens ship in GAMES/HEXA.By yaz@phoenix.oulu.fi (University of Oulu), posted to alt.sources, 1993.Originals in SRC/hexa/ORIG.